WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.450
Welcome to the lesson! Today we will look at
operations on matrices.

2
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:14.170
Operation: matrix addition. The operation of
adding matrices

3
00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:18.270
is defined only for matrices of the same size.

4
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.418
The sum of matrices A and B is the matrix
whose

5
00:00:22.418 --> 00:00:25.360
entries equal the sums of the entries

6
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.080
of A and B in the corresponding positions.

7
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.684
Now let us apply this formula to an example.

8
00:00:36.684 --> 00:00:42.740
Let two matrices be given. Their sizes are the
same, so

9
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:49.680
we can find their sum. We add the corresponding
entries of the matrices, row by row,

10
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.660
one after another. The sum of the matrices is
then this matrix.

11
00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.770
Operation: multiplying a matrix by a number.

12
00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:10.420
To multiply a matrix by a number, multiply
every entry of the matrix by that number.

13
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.203
Let us apply this formula to an example.

14
00:01:16.203 --> 00:01:22.880
A matrix is given and must be multiplied by
three. We multiply each of its entries by three.

15
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.020
The calculation gives this matrix.

16
00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.289
It is important to know that matrices can be
multiplied

17
00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:41.320
only when the number of columns of the first
matrix

18
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:48.000
equals the number of rows of the second.
Multiplying a matrix by a matrix

19
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.360
gives a matrix each entry of which equals the
sum of the

20
00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.480
products of the entries in row i of the first
matrix

21
00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:02.320
and the corresponding entries in column j of
the second matrix.

22
00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:35.470
The first matrix has two columns.

23
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.110
The second matrix has two rows.

24
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.260
So the product of A and B is defined.

25
00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:49.205
First, the entries of the first row of the
first matrix

26
00:02:49.205 --> 00:02:51.890
are multiplied by the corresponding entries

27
00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.497
of the first column of the second matrix.

28
00:02:54.497 --> 00:02:57.930
Then the entries of the second row of the
first matrix

29
00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.564
are multiplied by the corresponding entries of
the first

30
00:03:01.564 --> 00:03:04.420
column of the second matrix. In the same way

31
00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.920
we multiply the remaining entries.

32
00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:16.240
To sum up: in this lesson we learned to add
and multiply matrices.
